cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use benchsiDE, please cite it as below."
title: "benchsiDE: validated, client-side RNA-seq differential expression and discovery analysis"
version: 1.0.0-rc.2
date-released: "2026-10-04"
abstract: >-
  benchsiDE is a single-file web application for bulk RNA-seq analysis that runs
  entirely in the browser; expression data are not transmitted. It implements TMM
  normalization, filterByExpr filtering, moderated t, voom and covariate models,
  moderated F, interaction contrasts, gene-set testing (over-representation, GSEA,
  CAMERA, FRY), module discovery and cross-dataset comparison with random-effects
  meta-analysis (REML, Hartung-Knapp) and human-mouse homology families. Each statistical routine is validated
  against its reference implementation (edgeR, limma, metafor, RRHO, RNASeqPower,
  scipy, statsmodels) by an in-browser self-test and by an external validation on a public
  dataset (GEO GSE63310).
authors:
